  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "mYNj5BqStcdoQuQFPiK2YQR5RtI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:36:15.647Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The mutation is a thin translator\n\nA GraphQL mutation in a Powerhouse subgraph does not write a row. It builds an **action** and hands it to the Reactor. The Reactor runs the action through the reducer, stamps it as an operation, appends it to the document's history, and syncs it to connected peers. Everything that makes a Powerhouse write auditable happens *after* the resolver returns control.\n\nThe academy lesson sketches it schematically as a `dispatch` call:\n\n```ts\nMutation: {\n  async addTodo(_parent, { input }, ctx) {\n    return ctx.reactor.dispatch(\"<doc-id>\", [\n      { type: \"ADD_TODO\", input }\n    ]);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRead that as pseudocode for the shape, not as the live API. In `packages/reactor-api` the generated document-model resolvers do the same thing through the reactor client:\n\n```ts\nconst action = this.documentModel.actions[camelCase(op.name)];\nconst updatedDoc = await this.reactorClient.execute(\n  effectiveDocId,\n  \"main\",     // branch\n  [action(input)],\n);\nreturn toGqlPhDocument(updatedDoc);\n```\n\nNote `action(input)` \u2014 the resolver calls the model's **generated action creator**, so scope and action type come from the document model rather than from a hand-written literal. Custom subgraphs reach the same client as `subgraph.reactorClient`.\n\n## What follows from this\n\nThree consequences worth holding onto:\n\n1. **Validation is not the resolver's job.** The reducer owns it. A mutation that passes GraphQL type-checking can still be rejected by the reducer, and the rejection is recorded rather than silently dropped.\n2. **There is no write path that bypasses history.** Because the mutation goes through the Reactor, a GraphQL-authored change is indistinguishable from a Connect-authored one in the operation log.\n3. **Every mutation is inherently synced.** You do not publish an event after writing; the append *is* the event.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/06-switchboard/02-subgraphs.mdx, packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/document-model-subgraph.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:36:14.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:36:15.647Z"
    }
  },
